.TH CRUNCH_PPOLL 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
crunch_ppoll \- Linux x86-64 syscall 271
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/syscall_260_299.h>
.B int crunch_ppoll(struct pollfd* descriptors, nfds_t count, struct timespec* timeout, const sigset_t* mask);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Invokes raw ppoll with an eight-byte kernel signal set. The kernel may modify timeout, including on interruption.
This is a direct Linux x86-64 syscall wrapper; availability and permissions depend on the kernel and security policy.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ppoll (2)
